    <briefdescription>
<para>Abstract interface of a meshfree approximation, which evaluates shape functions from a set of kernels. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Given an evaluation point <formula id="5">$ \boldsymbol{x} $</formula> and a list of <formula id="77">$ n $</formula> candidate kernel functions <formula id="163">$ \phi_A $</formula>, <formula id="164">$ A = 0, \dots, n-1 $</formula> (<ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_discretizations_1_1_meshfree_1_1_kernel_function" kindref="compound">KernelFunction</ref>), an approximation computes the shape functions <formula id="165">$ \Psi_A(\boldsymbol{x}) $</formula> and/or their gradients. The output arrays are indexed by the position of the kernel in the candidate list; candidates that do not cover <formula id="5">$ \boldsymbol{x} $</formula> get zero entries.</para>
<para>The gradient output is a column-major <formula id="166">$ d \times n $</formula> array, i.e., entry <formula id="167">$ i + d\,A $</formula> holds <formula id="168">$ \partial \Psi_A / \partial x_i $</formula>, where <formula id="4">$ d $</formula> is the spatial dimension. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
